# 20. Trade-Off Analysis

## Accuracy

✅ Simple  
❌ Misleading for imbalanced datasets

---

## Precision

✅ Reduces false positives  
❌ May miss actual positive cases

---

## Recall

✅ Finds more actual positives  
❌ Can increase false positives

---

## F1

✅ Balances precision and recall  
❌ Doesn't encode every business cost

---

## ROC-AUC

✅ Threshold-independent ranking measure  
❌ Can appear optimistic for highly imbalanced problems

---

## PR-AUC

✅ Focuses on positive-class performance  
❌ Baseline depends on class prevalence and interpretation can be less intuitive

---

# 21. Future Enhancements & Production Improvements

Professional ML systems often add:

### 🔹 Cost-Sensitive Learning

Different errors receive different costs.

Example:

```text
False Negative Fraud → ₹100,000 loss
False Positive → ₹50 investigation cost
```

The system should account for this difference.

---

### 🔹 Probability Calibration

A model predicting:

```text
0.80 probability
```

should ideally be correct around 80% of the time for similarly scored cases.

Common approaches:

- Platt scaling
- Isotonic regression

---

### 🔹 Continuous Monitoring

After deployment, monitor:

- Precision
- Recall
- Drift
- Data quality
- Prediction distribution
- Business KPIs

Because a good model today may degrade tomorrow.

